  "label": "User projected onto the visual representation of emotional overwhelm",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the person covering their face with hands and showing a distressed eye, as this visual is used to represent the emotional state described in the text 'white kids be like \"i have had enough\"'. The user sees themselves or identifies with the emotional state being portrayed, even though the text targets a specific racialized group. The projection is onto the visual material (person) which serves as a metaphor for the group's supposed emotional burden.",
